                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "232780634",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198301708380",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 540,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 483,
                            "last_played": 1786851091
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I f**king love this game, and I've yet to beat it- Though I do love beating my head at this wall over and over again and learning new things each time. When/If I beat the game and if remember to update my review, I will.\n\nAt time of writing I have less than 10 hours, BUT I have a handful of hours on the PS4 version as well. Most of my hours were/are there still. \n\nThings of note:\n- You need to play w/ controller, preferably one w/ rumble vibrations like a dual shock PS4 controller honestly. This is because there are some small enemies that can be hard to see when they attach to the player's body and deal damage. If you have a rumble controller, it'll buzz telling you there is a lil guy on yah.\n- The death pits suck, no they don't get easier imo\n- I still have no idea how to deal with the poison and lava flooring on some sections\n- The co-op seems to be local only, but that is okay\n- There are lots of moving pieces to manage like food, health, mana, special attack charge, inventory space, potion materials, etc. \n\nYou WILL (or should) continue to improve the more you play, and its a lot of fun :D",
